Like, when we dented the car with the watermelon, you have to get the car fixed.
就像我们用西瓜把车砸凹了，你就得把车修好。

660
00:26:26.420 --> 00:26:26.700
Yes.
是的。

661
00:26:27.160 --> 00:26:28.240
You have to repair it.
你必须修理它。

662
00:26:28.320 --> 00:26:29.000
That's a rental.
还有租车费用。

663
00:26:29.260 --> 00:26:30.780
You have to return, right?
你得还车，对吧？

664
00:26:31.600 --> 00:26:34.740
And also, do you remember the cold open from Prince Family Paper?
还有，你还记得《王子纸业公司》那一集的前情提要冷开场吗？

665
00:26:35.280 --> 00:26:37.220
Lady, I had forgotten about this cold open.
天哪，我都把这段冷开场给忘了。

666
00:26:37.340 --> 00:26:40.760
I always remember that episode because it's like, oh, it breaks my heart.
我一直记得那一集，因为感觉，噢，它让我心碎。

667
00:26:40.880 --> 00:26:42.220
That's my Scott's Tots.
那是我的“斯科特的小宝贝们”。

668
00:26:42.400 --> 00:26:42.680
Right?
对吧？

669
00:26:42.860 --> 00:26:44.800
That's my cringe one that I can't watch.
那是我根本没法看的尴尬集数。

670
00:26:44.820 --> 00:26:46.040
It just breaks your heart.
它真的让人心碎。

671
00:26:46.040 --> 00:26:49.720
But I forgot about the prank at the beginning.
但我忘了开始时的恶作剧。

672
00:26:50.100 --> 00:26:51.720
Jim sets up this elaborate prank.
吉姆布下了这个精心策划的恶作剧。

673
00:26:51.940 --> 00:26:52.260
You know what?
你知道吗？

674
00:26:52.260 --> 00:26:53.920
I pulled a clip to refresh your memory.
我剪辑了一段视频来帮你们恢复记忆。

675
00:26:57.350 --> 00:26:58.390
What's this?
这是什么？

676
00:27:00.360 --> 00:27:01.520
Looks like a red wire.
看起来像是一根红线。

677
00:27:02.280 --> 00:27:04.480
Oh, I wasn't here before.
哦，以前这儿没有。

678
00:27:05.620 --> 00:27:06.740
It's a computer, Dwight.
这是台电脑，德怀特。

679
00:27:07.080 --> 00:27:08.240
I mean, computers have wires.
我的意思是，电脑都有线。

680
00:27:08.880 --> 00:27:09.520
Yours doesn't.
你的就没有。

681
00:27:10.700 --> 00:27:11.340
Doesn't it?
是吗？

682
00:27:12.280 --> 00:27:12.800
No.
没有。

683
00:27:14.840 --> 00:27:17.080
It's going in a different direction than the other wires.
它延伸的方向跟其他电线不一样。

684
00:27:17.520 --> 00:27:18.280
Dwight, I'm really busy.
德怀特，我真的很忙。

685
00:27:18.460 --> 00:27:19.500
I can't talk about this anymore.
我不能再跟你聊这个了。

686
00:27:22.730 --> 00:27:23.210
Dwight.
德怀特。

687
00:27:23.610 --> 00:27:24.810
Just shut up.
闭嘴就行。

688
00:27:24.830 --> 00:27:25.790
Shut up, Phyllis.
闭嘴，菲利斯。

689
00:27:28.580 --> 00:27:32.760
I got 500 feet of red wire at a flea market up by Dunmore High School.
我在邓莫尔高中附近的跳蚤市场买到了500英尺的红线。

690
00:27:33.540 --> 00:27:34.960
20 bucks for the whole spool.
整整一卷只要20块钱。

691
00:27:35.800 --> 00:27:36.240
Crazy.
太疯狂了。

692
00:27:36.520 --> 00:27:37.040
What a deal.
真是划算。

693
00:27:38.780 --> 00:27:40.380
Oh, he'll be fine.
哦，他会没事的。

694
00:27:40.600 --> 00:27:41.380
I made it up there.
我把它拉到那儿了。

695
00:27:41.840 --> 00:27:42.640
All right, Jim.
好吧，吉姆。

696
00:27:43.000 --> 00:27:46.760
You got $20 worth of red wire, right?
你花了20美元买红线，对吧？

697
00:27:47.040 --> 00:27:47.320
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

698
00:27:47.860 --> 00:27:51.540
He still had to run it through the entire office, under Phyllis's desk,
他还得把它拉过整个办公室，从菲利斯的办公桌底下穿过，

699
00:27:51.720 --> 00:27:56.160
around the corner, down the hall, out of the building, up a telephone pole?
绕过拐角，穿过走廊，出大楼，爬上电线杆？

700
00:27:56.320 --> 00:27:57.620
Yeah, how'd he get up there?
对啊，他是怎么爬上去的？

701
00:27:57.620 --> 00:27:58.040
Yeah.
对。

702
00:27:58.700 --> 00:28:01.280
I mean, here's what it really coSt.
我的意思是，这才是它真正的成本。

703
00:28:01.460 --> 00:28:05.160
First of all, they had to put all the stunt throughout the office, right?
首先，他们得把所有的特技道具放满整个办公室，对吧？

704
00:28:05.300 --> 00:28:05.520
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

705
00:28:05.520 --> 00:28:06.100
They had to do that.
他们必须得这么做。

706
00:28:06.660 --> 00:28:10.020
Then they had to build a safe pole in the parking lot.
然后他们得在停车场建一个安全的电线杆。

707
00:28:10.100 --> 00:28:11.340
They had to build a whole pole.
他们得建一个完整的电线杆。

708
00:28:11.720 --> 00:28:12.420
Then they had to have—
然后他们还得——

709
00:28:12.420 --> 00:28:12.470
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

710
00:28:12.520 --> 00:28:14.880
He couldn't climb up a real utility pole.
他不能爬一根真正的电线杆。

711
00:28:14.880 --> 00:28:15.860
No, of course not.
不，当然不能。

712
00:28:16.120 --> 00:28:19.720
And then Rain had to climb it, so then they had to get a green screen,
然后雷恩必须爬上去，所以他们得弄一个绿幕，

713
00:28:20.100 --> 00:28:21.260
do all the compositing.
做所有的后期合成。

714
00:28:21.620 --> 00:28:23.440
All in, it was $16,500.
总共花了 16,500 美元。

715
00:28:24.080 --> 00:28:25.480
Not 20 bucks, Jim.
可不是 20 块钱，吉姆。

716
00:28:26.120 --> 00:28:26.560
Yeah.
对。

717
00:28:27.280 --> 00:28:31.400
Jim's pranks did not cost Jim a lot, but they cost us a lot.
吉姆的恶作剧没有花吉姆很多钱，但它们花在我们很多钱上。

718
00:28:32.140 --> 00:28:33.020
You know what I'm saying?
你知道我在说什么吗？

719
00:28:33.360 --> 00:28:35.560
They cost the office production a lot.
它们让办公室制作成本损失惨重。

720
00:28:35.700 --> 00:28:36.020
They did.
确实如此。

721
00:28:36.240 --> 00:28:40.660
I wonder if NBC execs would see, like, a Jim prank in a cold open and be like,
我在想，NBC 的高管们在冷场开场里看到吉姆的恶作剧时，会不会觉得，

722
00:28:40.660 --> 00:28:41.280
s**t.
操。

723
00:28:41.440 --> 00:28:41.920
Yeah.
对。

724
00:28:42.700 --> 00:28:43.240
Damn it.
该死。

725
00:28:43.600 --> 00:28:45.020
Pam Putsch would be like, ah.
帕姆·普特施可能会觉得，啊。

726
00:28:45.420 --> 00:28:45.940
Exactly.
没错。

727
00:28:46.420 --> 00:28:51.620
Well, you know, do you remember when we did our Office Ladies Live fan mailbag episode?
好吧，你知道的，还记得我们做“办公室女士”现场粉丝信箱那一期吗？

728
00:28:51.880 --> 00:28:58.920
There was a fan, Joe V from Oregon, and he broke down every single one of Jim's pranks
有个粉丝，来自俄勒冈州的乔·V，他详细剖析了吉姆对德怀特做的每一个恶作剧

729
00:28:58.920 --> 00:28:59.660
on Dwight.
针对德怀特。

730
00:28:59.840 --> 00:29:00.920
Yes, that's right.
对，没错。

731
00:29:01.220 --> 00:29:02.020
With, like, real numbers.
而且是用那种真实的数字。

732
00:29:02.200 --> 00:29:02.680
Let me look.
让我看看。

733
00:29:02.780 --> 00:29:03.260
Hold on.
等等。

734
00:29:03.840 --> 00:29:04.820
I'm going to go.
我要去了。

735
00:29:05.080 --> 00:29:06.140
Pull it up, lady.
把它调出来，女士。

736
00:29:06.180 --> 00:29:07.100
I'm going to pull this up.
我要把它调出来。

737
00:29:07.100 --> 00:29:10.120
That was amazing, like, detail and accounting by Joe.
乔的细节和记账真是太惊人了。

738
00:29:10.340 --> 00:29:10.700
Yes.
对。

739
00:29:10.840 --> 00:29:21.900
So, he estimated that Jim spent $1,809.11 on pranking Dwight over the nine seasons.
所以，他估计吉姆在九季中恶作剧德怀特花了 1,809.11 美元。

740
00:29:21.900 --> 00:29:22.800
Hmm.
嗯。

741
00:29:23.060 --> 00:29:28.760
And he estimated that the most expensive prank was the tearaway suit.
他估计最贵的恶作剧是那个撕裂西装。

742
00:29:28.960 --> 00:29:29.160
Hmm.
嗯。

743
00:29:29.500 --> 00:29:31.040
That would have cost him the moSt.
那个花费他最多。

744
00:29:31.160 --> 00:29:32.460
And we go into it in this episode.
我们在这集里会深入探讨。

745
00:29:32.560 --> 00:29:38.940
He has a whole breakdown of exactly how much everything cost, in his estimation, if Jim
他有一个完整的明细，精确估算了每样东西花了多少钱，如果吉姆

746
00:29:38.940 --> 00:29:41.180
was real crafty, you know.
真的很狡猾的话，你知道的。

747
00:29:41.340 --> 00:29:41.600
Yeah.
对。

748
00:29:41.720 --> 00:29:47.520
He didn't pay a set construction team to make a desk and wrap it in wrapping paper.
他没有花钱请布景搭建团队来做一个桌子并用包装纸包起来。

749
00:29:47.720 --> 00:29:49.200
He didn't build a fakie pole.
他没有建一个假的电线杆。

750
00:29:49.360 --> 00:29:51.300
He didn't, yeah, build a utility pole.
他没有，对，建一根电线杆。

751
00:29:51.300 --> 00:29:56.140
Yeah, like, he takes Jim at his word and says, okay, sure, Jim, that prank with the
对，就是那种，他把吉姆的话当真了，然后说，好吧，当然，吉姆，那个

752
00:29:56.140 --> 00:29:59.040
red wire cost you $20 and a lot of effort.
红线恶作剧花掉了你20美元和很多心血。

753
00:29:59.340 --> 00:29:59.780
Yeah.
没错。

754
00:30:00.180 --> 00:30:01.640
Oh, that's the other thing that I love.
哦，这也是我喜欢的另一个点。

755
00:30:02.120 --> 00:30:07.960
Joe said, I'm not counting, like, his sweat equity.
乔说，我没把他的汗水投资算进去。

756
00:30:08.160 --> 00:30:10.620
Like, I'm not counting the cost of his time.
比如，我没有计算他付出时间的成本。

757
00:30:10.900 --> 00:30:11.060
Yeah.
对。

758
00:30:11.200 --> 00:30:12.360
Which is clearly a lot.
而这显然非常多。

759
00:30:12.600 --> 00:30:12.940
Yeah.
对。

760
00:30:13.300 --> 00:30:14.560
He got that for free.
他那是白得的。

761
00:30:14.760 --> 00:30:16.760
Think about what Jim could have done with that money.
想想吉姆用这笔钱本来能做成什么。

762
00:30:17.060 --> 00:30:17.700
Like, maybe.
比如，也许。

763
00:30:18.020 --> 00:30:18.460
Oh.
哦。

764
00:30:18.560 --> 00:30:20.980
Maybe they didn't have to buy his parents' place.
也许他们就不用买他父母的房子了。

765
00:30:21.300 --> 00:30:21.600
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

766
00:30:22.220 --> 00:30:22.660
Yeah.
对。

767
00:30:22.740 --> 00:30:26.000
Maybe he didn't have to invest their savings in his company.
也许他就不用把他们的积蓄投进他的公司里了。

768
00:30:26.200 --> 00:30:27.100
Oh, yeah, because.
哦，对，因为。

769
00:30:27.580 --> 00:30:29.200
They would have had some extra money.
他们本来可以有一些额外的钱。

770
00:30:29.380 --> 00:30:29.480
Yeah.
对。

771
00:30:29.940 --> 00:30:30.220
Yeah.
对。

772
00:30:30.960 --> 00:30:35.740
Just a thought, Jim, about how you spend your family's money.
只是个想法，吉姆，关于你是怎么花你家里的钱的。

773
00:30:36.180 --> 00:30:36.540
All right.
好吧。

774
00:30:36.640 --> 00:30:38.620
I think that brings us to season six.
我想这就说到第六季了。

775
00:30:38.620 --> 00:30:39.400
It does.
确实。

776
00:30:40.000 --> 00:30:45.340
And season six had a lot of episodes that went over our usual budget.
而且第六季有很多集的预算超出了我们平常的标准。

777
00:30:45.720 --> 00:30:50.740
This is not confirmed, but in looking at all of this accounting, dare I say, season six
这虽然未经证实，但在查看所有这些账目后，我敢说，第六季

778
00:30:50.740 --> 00:30:52.180
might have been our most expensive.
可能是我们最贵的一季。

779
00:30:52.480 --> 00:30:52.860
Ooh.
噢。

780
00:30:52.860 --> 00:30:58.760
For example, the delivery parts one and two, they had to build the whole hospital set, as
比如，《分娩（上下集）》，他们必须搭建整个医院布景，

781
00:30:58.760 --> 00:31:01.480
well as Jim and Pam's kitchen that Dwight then demolishes.
还有吉姆和帕姆的厨房，后来被德怀特给拆了。

782
00:31:01.820 --> 00:31:03.460
We have Andy's play.
还有安迪的戏剧。

783
00:31:03.740 --> 00:31:09.860
This had major music and licensing fees, a live orchestra, lots of additional caSt.
这有大笔的音乐和版权费用、现场乐队、大量额外的演员。

784
00:31:09.860 --> 00:31:17.620
And just to fill the theater with background performers for Andy's play, that cost over
而且光是为了给安迪的戏剧填满剧院的背景演员，就花了

785
00:31:17.620 --> 00:31:18.700
$75,000.
75000多美元。

786
00:31:19.160 --> 00:31:19.560
Wow.
哇。

787
00:31:19.980 --> 00:31:23.180
And then, who can forget Threat Level Midnight?
然后，谁能忘记《威胁级别：午夜》呢？

788
00:31:23.180 --> 00:31:29.600
You guys, when Randy emailed us about it, he literally wrote, whoa, this one was a doozy!
伙计们，当兰迪给我们发邮件时，他简直是这么写的：哇，这一集可真够劲！

789
00:31:29.820 --> 00:31:31.120
Exclamation point.
感叹号。

790
00:31:31.380 --> 00:31:32.540
It sure was.
确实如此。

791
00:31:32.540 --> 00:31:39.720
We had guest cast extras, locations, transportation, an ice rink, minor skaters.
我们有客串演员、群众演员、外景、交通、溜冰场、少年滑冰运动员。

792
00:31:40.100 --> 00:31:45.240
Anytime someone is a kid, it's more expensive because you have to add the cost of the child
只要涉及小孩，成本就会更高，因为你必须加上儿童

793
00:31:45.240 --> 00:31:46.540
advocate and the tutor.
权益代表和家庭教师的费用。

794
00:31:46.800 --> 00:31:50.600
There was also music, choreography, special effects, visual effects.
还有音乐、编舞、特效、视觉效果。

795
00:31:51.240 --> 00:31:54.960
That episode put us almost to half a million dollars over budget.
那一集让我们的预算超支了将近五十万美元。

796
00:31:55.180 --> 00:31:58.780
But Randy said, quote, this one had it all.
但兰迪原话说道：这一集应有尽有。

797
00:31:59.180 --> 00:32:01.620
I sure believe it was all worth it.
我深信这一切都是值得的。

798
00:32:01.760 --> 00:32:04.500
This episode consistently ranks as a fan favorite.
这一集一直名列粉丝最爱前茅。

799
00:32:04.800 --> 00:32:05.780
It does, Randy.
确实如此，兰迪。

800
00:32:05.980 --> 00:32:06.480
It does.
确实如此。

801
00:32:06.960 --> 00:32:10.100
God bless you for having to make that call to NBC.
感谢上帝替你给NBC打那个电话。

802
00:32:11.680 --> 00:32:16.140
This brings us, though, to the most expensive episode from season six.
不过，这也让我们想到了第六季中最贵的一集。

803
00:32:16.140 --> 00:32:22.680
Randy actually said it was the single most expensive episode that took place in his tenure.
兰迪实际上说过，这是他在任期间经历的单集成本最高的一集。

804
00:32:22.940 --> 00:32:23.880
Should we say it together?
我们要不要一起说出来？

805
00:32:25.220 --> 00:32:25.720
Niagara.
尼亚加拉瀑布。

806
00:32:26.380 --> 00:32:26.880
Yeah.
对。

807
00:32:27.280 --> 00:32:30.940
When we posed this question to all three of the fellas, Steve Burgess said,
当我们把这个问题抛给三位伙计时，史蒂夫·伯吉斯说，

808
00:32:31.120 --> 00:32:33.780
the first thing that jumps to mind is the Niagara episode.
脑海中浮现的第一件事就是《尼亚加拉瀑布》那一集。

809
00:32:34.180 --> 00:32:38.160
Randy was producing, but I was the UPM and I was working with the budget.
兰迪当时是制片人，而我是制片主任，我在处理预算。

810
00:32:38.160 --> 00:32:46.360
If you remember, he said, we first thought Dwight was going to ride a horse over the falls.
如果你还记得的话，他说，我们起初以为德怀特要骑着马冲过瀑布。

811
00:32:46.440 --> 00:32:46.940
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

812
00:32:47.240 --> 00:32:50.460
We talked quite a bit about that when we broke down this episode.
我们在剖析这一集时，讨论了不少这方面的内容。

813
00:32:50.460 --> 00:32:52.480
It was a whole storyline that Greg had.
那是格雷格构思的整条故事线。

814
00:32:52.680 --> 00:32:53.700
It didn't end up happening.
最后没拍成。

815
00:32:53.940 --> 00:32:57.860
But they did have to do all of this prep towards that story.
但他们确实为那个故事做了所有的前期准备。

816
00:32:58.180 --> 00:33:00.800
Oh, lady, we talk about it in the episode.
天哪，我们在节目里聊过这个。

817
00:33:00.980 --> 00:33:05.040
They trained a horse to jump into water.
他们训练了一匹马跳进水里。

818
00:33:05.180 --> 00:33:05.460
Yes.
是的。

819
00:33:05.760 --> 00:33:07.400
Over on the Paramount lot.
就在派拉蒙的外景地。

820
00:33:07.400 --> 00:33:11.980
But that huge, giant parking lot that they can fill with water to make it look like an ocean.
就是那个可以注满水，看起来像大海的巨大停车场。

821
00:33:12.180 --> 00:33:12.480
Yes.
是的。

822
00:33:12.620 --> 00:33:14.460
I think they used it in that Jim Carrey movie.
我想他们在金·凯瑞的那部电影里用过它。

823
00:33:14.660 --> 00:33:14.960
Yes.
对。

824
00:33:15.560 --> 00:33:16.420
What's that one?
那是哪部？

825
00:33:16.540 --> 00:33:17.160
Bruce Almighty?
《冒牌天神》？

826
00:33:17.500 --> 00:33:17.820
No.
不是。

827
00:33:19.700 --> 00:33:20.480
Liar Liar?
《大话王》？

828
00:33:20.620 --> 00:33:20.900
No.
不是。

829
00:33:21.120 --> 00:33:23.520
What's the one where he doesn't know he's in a reality show?
他不知道自己身处真人秀的那部叫什么？

830
00:33:23.680 --> 00:33:24.640
The Truman Show?
《楚门的世界》？

831
00:33:24.780 --> 00:33:25.700
Truman Show!
《楚门的世界》！

832
00:33:26.540 --> 00:33:30.220
Don't quote me on that, but I think that's the place they did that.
别咬定我说得对，但我觉着他们就是在那拍的。

833
00:33:30.440 --> 00:33:32.860
Anyway, back on topic here.
言归正传。

834
00:33:33.000 --> 00:33:36.060
Side note, I don't know if you've watched The Truman Show lately.
顺便说一句，我不知道你最近有没有看《楚门的世界》。

835
00:33:36.060 --> 00:33:37.660
It really holds up.
它真的很经久不衰。

836
00:33:37.800 --> 00:33:40.640
It is really moving and still really funny.
它真的很感人，而且依然非常搞笑。

837
00:33:40.880 --> 00:33:42.060
It's super, super good.
超级超级棒。

838
00:33:42.460 --> 00:33:42.840
No.
没有。

839
00:33:42.980 --> 00:33:43.900
How's it that you've seen it?
你怎么会看过？

840
00:33:43.960 --> 00:33:45.280
I haven't seen it in years.
我都好几年没看了。

841
00:33:45.380 --> 00:33:46.680
We showed it to our son.
我们把它放给儿子看了。

842
00:33:46.880 --> 00:33:47.300
Oh.
哦。

843
00:33:47.520 --> 00:33:50.520
We're looking for, like, good movies that we could watch together.
我们在找那种适合一起看的佳片。

844
00:33:50.760 --> 00:33:53.100
Also, I thought Forrest Gump held up really well.
另外，我觉得《阿甘正传》也非常经久不衰。

845
00:33:53.100 --> 00:33:54.520
Yeah, we watched that one, too.
对，我们也看过那部。

846
00:33:54.540 --> 00:33:54.940
It did.
确实如此。

847
00:33:55.260 --> 00:33:55.500
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

848
00:33:55.620 --> 00:33:57.580
There's a couple that didn't, but I won't call them out.
有些电影经不起时间考验，但我不会点名批评它们。

849
00:33:57.720 --> 00:34:00.860
I'm not going to say if you didn't hold up, but I am going to shout you out if you do.
如果没经受住时间的考验，我不会说出来；但要是经受住了，我一定会夸夸它们。

850
00:34:01.300 --> 00:34:01.960
Okay, good.
好吧，不错。

851
00:34:02.520 --> 00:34:07.380
Yeah, we watched one recently that did not hold up, and there were so many boobs, and
对啊，我们最近看了一部，完全经不起时代考验，里面有超多露胸镜头，而且

852
00:34:07.380 --> 00:34:08.500
I forgot there were boobs.
我都忘了以前有这么多露胸镜头。

853
00:34:08.500 --> 00:34:11.060
Oh, my God, the amount of gratuitous boobs in movies.
天呐，电影里莫名其妙的露胸镜头也太多了吧。

854
00:34:11.060 --> 00:34:14.340
There was just a whole decade of boobs just everywhere.
简直有一整十年，到处都是这种镜头。

855
00:34:14.560 --> 00:34:15.920
Yes, I know.
没错，我知道。

856
00:34:16.040 --> 00:34:17.020
We grew up with that.
我们就是看着那些长大的。

857
00:34:17.180 --> 00:34:19.440
We grew up with gratuitous boobs in movies.
我们是看着电影里那些莫名其妙的露胸镜头长大的。

858
00:34:19.540 --> 00:34:19.820
Yeah.
对啊。

859
00:34:20.140 --> 00:34:20.740
I know.
我知道。

860
00:34:20.840 --> 00:34:21.480
And I forgot.
我都给忘了。

861
00:34:21.740 --> 00:34:22.480
I was like, oh, my God.
当时我就想，我的天呐。

862
00:34:22.920 --> 00:34:23.100
Ha!
哈！

863
00:34:23.380 --> 00:34:24.240
Anyway, okay.
总之，好吧。

864
00:34:24.480 --> 00:34:27.800
Even my beloved diehard has a gratuitous boob in the beginning.
就连我深爱的《虎胆龙威》开头都有莫名其妙的露胸镜头。

865
00:34:27.960 --> 00:34:28.420
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

866
00:34:28.880 --> 00:34:29.180
Yeah.
对啊。

867
00:34:29.680 --> 00:34:30.540
It's too bad.
太遗憾了。

868
00:34:30.880 --> 00:34:31.160
Okay.
好吧。

869
00:34:31.160 --> 00:34:36.300
Anyway, back to Niagara, where there were no boobs, but there was maybe going to be a
言归正传，说回《尼亚加拉》，那里倒没有什么露胸镜头，但可能有一匹

870
00:34:36.300 --> 00:34:38.120
horse go over a fall.
马要掉下瀑布。

871
00:34:38.640 --> 00:34:44.200
So Steve said, when we had the table read for the episode, our NBC execs asked me if we were
所以史蒂夫说，当我们为这集进行围读时，NBC的高管问我，我们是不是

872
00:34:44.200 --> 00:34:47.500
a million over budget, and I was happy to say no.
超预算了一百万，我很高兴地说没有。

873
00:34:49.020 --> 00:34:50.800
Only $975,000 over.
只超了975,000美元。

874
00:34:51.040 --> 00:34:53.700
They laughed and said, yep, a million over.
他们笑着说，没错，就是超了一百万。

875
00:34:53.900 --> 00:34:54.300
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

876
00:34:54.300 --> 00:35:01.640
That said, I guess Randy Cordray still had to really fight to have that skeleton crew
尽管如此，我猜兰迪·科德雷还是得据理力争，才能让那个精简剧组

877
00:35:01.640 --> 00:35:06.920
go to the actual Niagara Falls because NBC wanted you to shoot it on a blue screen.
去真正的尼亚加拉大瀑布实景拍摄，因为NBC原本想让你们在蓝幕前拍。

878
00:35:07.140 --> 00:35:07.560
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

879
00:35:07.820 --> 00:35:12.140
And Steve said, we all agreed that would have looked like crap, and ultimately Randy won
史蒂夫说，我们都一致认为那样拍出来会像狗屎一样，最终兰迪赢得了

880
00:35:12.140 --> 00:35:13.800
the fight to shoot on location.
去实景拍摄的抗争。

881
00:35:14.360 --> 00:35:14.740
Yeah.
对啊。

882
00:35:14.940 --> 00:35:23.400
Randy told me that the New York Niagara Falls unit cost, oh, right around $122,000.
兰迪告诉我，去纽约尼亚加拉瀑布外景组的费用大概在122,000美元左右。

883
00:35:23.400 --> 00:35:28.080
There were also several episodes this season that I would not have guessed would have come
这个季度还有好几集，我根本猜不到

884
00:35:28.080 --> 00:35:29.480
with such a big ticket price.
制作成本会这么高。

885
00:35:29.760 --> 00:35:36.360
For example, Randy also said, surprisingly, Koi Pine was a very expensive episode.
比如，兰迪还说，出人意料的是，《锦鲤池》是一集非常昂贵的剧集。

886
00:35:36.700 --> 00:35:40.660
Think about the set construction, the decoration for the Koi Pine.
想想看布景的搭建，还有锦鲤池的装饰。

887
00:35:40.860 --> 00:35:42.620
All of that was around $80,000.
光是那些就大约花了80,000美元。

888
00:35:43.200 --> 00:35:47.720
The Koi Fish provided by the Animal Trainers were about $17,000.
由动物驯兽师提供的锦鲤大约花了17,000美元。

889
00:35:48.360 --> 00:35:51.320
Costumes for that Halloween cold open were around $32,000.
万圣节那个开场戏的服装大约花了32,000美元。

890
00:35:51.320 --> 00:35:53.560
And then it aired, but then was ultimately cut.
结果播了之后，最后却被删减了。

891
00:35:53.920 --> 00:35:55.440
Yeah, that's right.
对，没错。

892
00:35:55.720 --> 00:35:57.760
So that rounds out to an expensive episode.
所以总算下来，这确实是一集花钱很多的剧。

893
00:35:58.460 --> 00:36:01.520
Well, Randy also mentioned shareholder meeting.
对了，兰迪还提到了《股东大会》。

894
00:36:01.920 --> 00:36:06.300
He said that the scenes on location downtown were expensive.
他说在市中心实景拍摄的场景很贵。

895
00:36:06.800 --> 00:36:12.200
Also, they had to factor in transportation costs, the large number of background performers.
而且，他们还得把交通成本、大量的背景演员都计算在内。

896
00:36:12.200 --> 00:36:14.580
And I did not know this.
而且我之前不知道这个。

897
00:36:14.720 --> 00:36:18.460
We needed an extra day of filming to finish that episode.
我们为了拍完那一集，额外多需要了一天拍摄时间。

898
00:36:18.660 --> 00:36:23.120
While we would normally have five days to finish an episode, this one took six.
平时我们通常有五天时间拍完一集，但这一集花了六天。

899
00:36:23.360 --> 00:36:24.480
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

900
00:36:24.500 --> 00:36:26.240
I also didn't know this.
我以前也不知道这个。

901
00:36:26.580 --> 00:36:29.900
Another episode from season six helped to balance the books,
第六季的另一集有助于收支平衡，

902
00:36:29.900 --> 00:36:33.120
and it was none other than Scott's Tots.
它正是《斯科特的 Tots》。

903
00:36:33.980 --> 00:36:40.120
That one was originally budgeted pretty high because of the choreographer, dancers, extras, locations.
那一集最初预算相当高，因为有编舞、舞者、群演和外景。

904
00:36:40.580 --> 00:36:42.040
But director B.J.
但导演 B.J.

905
00:36:42.160 --> 00:36:47.460
Novak was so efficient that they finished his episode in only four days.
诺瓦克非常高效，他们在短短四天内就拍完了他那一集。

906
00:36:47.460 --> 00:36:49.600
He finished a whole day early.
他整整提前了一天完成。

907
00:36:49.920 --> 00:36:54.860
So that helped balance the books for that extra day that they needed for shareholder meeting.
所以这有助于平衡股东大会所需的那额外一天的预算。

908
00:36:55.060 --> 00:37:01.500
I'm so curious if B.J is the only director in the history of the office that got his episode in in four days.
我很好奇 B.J 是不是《办公室》历史上唯一一个在四天内完成拍摄的导演。

909
00:37:01.500 --> 00:37:03.600
Oh, that's a great question.
哦，这真是个好问题。

910
00:37:03.760 --> 00:37:04.060
Right?
对吧？

911
00:37:04.280 --> 00:37:06.920
I mean, that seems so difficult to do.
我的意思是，这看起来太难做到了。

912
00:37:07.140 --> 00:37:14.100
I feel like I remember a couple of times when we would come back to work after, like, a holiday weekend.
我觉得我记得有几次，我们在像长周末这样的假期之后回来工作。

913
00:37:14.500 --> 00:37:17.640
Like an MLK Day weekend or a President's weekend.
比如马丁·路德·金纪念日周末或总统日周末。

914
00:37:18.180 --> 00:37:21.780
And we were forced to shoot an episode in only four days.
我们被迫在短短四天内拍完一集。

915
00:37:21.940 --> 00:37:26.340
But they would plan it so that it was one of those, what did they call them, bottle episodes,
但他们会计划让它成为那种，他们叫什么来着，情景剧核心集，

916
00:37:26.340 --> 00:37:28.880
where they just took place in the office.
也就是只在办公室里发生的故事。

917
00:37:28.980 --> 00:37:29.220
Yeah.
对。

918
00:37:29.420 --> 00:37:30.540
No big stunts.
没有大特技。

919
00:37:30.540 --> 00:37:33.400
Like a conference room episode where we're just in there.
就像会议室那一集，我们就在里面。

920
00:37:33.560 --> 00:37:33.800
Right.
没错。

921
00:37:33.960 --> 00:37:34.100
Yeah.
对。

922
00:37:34.280 --> 00:37:35.960
And we could bang those out in four days.
我们可以在四天内搞定那些。

923
00:37:36.100 --> 00:37:36.300
Yeah.
是啊。

924
00:37:37.220 --> 00:37:39.600
Randy also shares a bunch of other tidbits from this season.
兰迪还分享了这一季的其他一些花絮。

925
00:37:39.600 --> 00:37:42.500
I just want to shout out just one or two randos.
我只想向一两个路人致敬。

926
00:37:42.680 --> 00:37:42.840
Ready?
准备好了吗？

927
00:37:43.080 --> 00:37:43.320
Okay.
好的。

928
00:37:43.900 --> 00:37:47.080
The swans for Secret Santa were $9,600.
《秘密圣诞老人》里的天鹅花了 9600 美元。

929
00:37:47.820 --> 00:37:51.760
In case you're wondering what it costs to put some swans in an episode.
如果你想知道在剧里放几只天鹅要花多少钱的话。

930
00:37:52.160 --> 00:37:55.780
Also, you remember Joe Bennett's Great Danes for Manager and Salesman?
还有，你还记得乔·贝内特在《经理与推销员》里的大丹犬吗？

931
00:37:55.880 --> 00:37:56.160
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

932
00:37:56.500 --> 00:38:00.020
For the week, those Great Danes were $21,000.
就那一周，那些大丹犬花了 21000 美元。

933
00:38:00.540 --> 00:38:01.540
My God.
天哪。

934
00:38:02.300 --> 00:38:04.760
Dogs and swans cost a lot, y'all.
狗和天鹅可真贵啊，各位。

935
00:38:05.240 --> 00:38:10.220
Finally, both Randy and Steve Burgess talked about what all went into the episode, garage sale.
最后，兰迪和史蒂夫·伯吉斯都谈到了《车库大甩卖》这一集所付出的努力。

936
00:38:10.740 --> 00:38:15.320
Randy said the Michael Holley proposal scene cost about $74,000.
兰迪说迈克尔·霍利的求婚场景花费大约 74000 美元。

937
00:38:15.320 --> 00:38:20.900
They had to strike the annex over a weekend, build a waterproof collecting pan underneath,
他们必须在周末拆除附楼，在下方建造一个防水收集盘，

938
00:38:21.200 --> 00:38:23.580
then rebuild and redress the annex.
然后重建并重新布置附楼。

939
00:38:23.800 --> 00:38:28.040
Once that was accomplished, Special Effects had to rig overhead sprinklers.
一旦完成，特效团队就必须安装头顶洒水器。

940
00:38:28.220 --> 00:38:34.600
They brought in this large warm water system so Steve and Amy wouldn't be completely doused in freezing cold water.
他们带来了一个大型温水系统，这样史蒂夫和艾米就不会被冰冷的水完全浇透。

941
00:38:35.260 --> 00:38:45.260
And Steve also went on to say, you guys, they had a second and third floor ready to go to replace if the sprinklers did ruin the floor in that first take.
史蒂夫接着说，伙计们，如果洒水器真的毁了第一条的地板，他们已经准备好了第二层和第三层来替换。

942
00:38:45.260 --> 00:38:46.540
But we didn't need it.
但我们没用上。

943
00:38:46.620 --> 00:38:47.440
They did it in one.
他们一遍就过了。

944
00:38:47.580 --> 00:38:48.240
Yeah, thankfully.
对，谢天谢地。

945
00:38:49.480 --> 00:38:52.120
All right, let's move into Seasons 8 and 9.
好了，让我们进入第八季和第九季。

946
00:38:52.540 --> 00:38:57.020
There was a very clear winner for Most Expensive Episode in Season 8.
第八季里最贵的一集有一个非常明显的赢家。

947
00:38:57.480 --> 00:38:59.780
I wasn't there, but you were there, Angela.
我不在场，但你在场，安吉拉。

948
00:39:00.040 --> 00:39:02.300
And it was Season 8 Pool Party.
那就是第八季的《泳池派对》。

949
00:39:02.300 --> 00:39:03.260
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

950
00:39:03.620 --> 00:39:08.300
For those of us that spent a week in that house and many days in the swimming pool,
对于我们这些在那栋房子里待了一周、在游泳池里待了好几天的人来说，

951
00:39:09.020 --> 00:39:10.340
that's what I want to say.
这就是我想说的。

952
00:39:10.860 --> 00:39:12.900
I mean, we will never forget pool party.
我是说，我们永远不会忘记泳池派对。

953
00:39:13.000 --> 00:39:14.360
It's kind of like a rite of passage.
这有点像是一种成人礼。

954
00:39:14.540 --> 00:39:16.560
Like, we still like, oh, remember being in the pool?
比如，我们还会说，哦，还记得在泳池里的时候吗？

955
00:39:16.960 --> 00:39:19.300
And I was in the pool with that prosthetic belly.
而且我当时还戴着那个假肚子在泳池里。

956
00:39:19.440 --> 00:39:20.480
Let's not forget that.
咱们可别忘了这一点。

957
00:39:21.080 --> 00:39:23.700
Steve said it was another very expensive episode.
史蒂夫说这是又一集非常昂贵的剧集。

958
00:39:24.200 --> 00:39:27.020
He said, if you remember when we first broke down this episode,
他说，如果你还记得我们第一次剖析这一集的时候，

959
00:39:27.200 --> 00:39:30.760
Steve shared with us that they couldn't find a house with a pool that worked.
史蒂夫跟我们分享说，他们当时找不到一栋带合适泳池的房子。

960
00:39:30.760 --> 00:39:35.720
So they shot the interior of the house in a different location from the house that had the pool
所以他们在一个地方拍了房子的内景，而泳池却在另一个地方的房子里，

961
00:39:35.720 --> 00:39:42.460
because Charles McDougal, the director, wanted an indoor pool, which apparently did not exiSt.
因为导演查尔斯·麦克杜格想要一个室内泳池，而这显然是不存在的。

962
00:39:42.720 --> 00:39:44.740
Well, very hard to find in Southern California.
好吧，在南加州很难找到。

963
00:39:45.000 --> 00:39:45.340
I know.
我知道。

964
00:39:45.460 --> 00:39:47.440
Who wants an indoor pool in Southern California?
谁会在南加州想要一个室内泳池啊？

965
00:39:47.620 --> 00:39:48.000
No one.
没有人。

966
00:39:48.700 --> 00:39:52.500
So they did find this house that had an indoor-outdoor pool,
所以他们确实找到了这样一栋房子，它有一个室内室外结合的泳池，

967
00:39:52.600 --> 00:39:58.780
but they had to have construction crews work around the clock to enclose the outdoor part of it
但他们不得不让施工队夜以继日地工作，把室外部分封闭起来，

968
00:39:58.780 --> 00:40:01.420
to make it look like it was a completely indoor pool.
好让它看起来像是一个完全的室内泳池。

969
00:40:01.620 --> 00:40:05.380
Steve shared pictures with us on how they stitched together the two different houses
史蒂夫跟我们分享了他们是如何把这两栋不同的房子拼凑在一起的照片，

970
00:40:05.380 --> 00:40:06.620
and all the work they did.
以及他们所做的大量工作。

971
00:40:07.060 --> 00:40:08.800
It was really wild.
