给你来个内裤楔进屁股。

1278
00:53:47.440 --> 00:53:48.160
I know.
我知道。

1279
00:53:48.240 --> 00:53:48.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1280
00:53:48.580 --> 00:53:51.480
And also just like, oh, are you in a bad mood?
还有就是，哦，你心情不好吗？

1281
00:53:51.640 --> 00:53:52.400
Tickle, tickle.
挠挠，挠挠。

1282
00:53:52.960 --> 00:53:54.660
I'm like, no, I'm like in a bad mood.
我就想说，不，我现在心情很不好。

1283
00:53:54.880 --> 00:54:00.080
I once dated a guy who when I was legitimately upset, like, oh, you were supposed to pick me
我曾和一个男生交往过，当我真的生气时，比如，哦，你应该来接我

1284
00:54:00.080 --> 00:54:01.000
up and you forgot.
却给忘了。

1285
00:54:01.320 --> 00:54:03.300
Like as Pam was in that episode.
就像那一集里的帕姆一样。

1286
00:54:03.500 --> 00:54:03.740
Yes.
对。

1287
00:54:03.860 --> 00:54:05.620
And then he would say this to me.
然后他会这样对我说。

1288
00:54:05.760 --> 00:54:07.620
He'd go, oh, anger.
他会说，哦，生气啦。

1289
00:54:08.280 --> 00:54:08.680
Oh.
哦。

1290
00:54:08.960 --> 00:54:09.280
Anger.
生气啦。

1291
00:54:09.620 --> 00:54:10.000
Oh, no.
哦，不。

1292
00:54:10.180 --> 00:54:12.680
And I was like, I am going to.
而我会说，我要……

1293
00:54:13.340 --> 00:54:14.900
You want to see anger?
想看真正的生气吗？

1294
00:54:15.400 --> 00:54:15.800
Yeah.
是啊。

1295
00:54:16.360 --> 00:54:16.840
Oh.
哦。

1296
00:54:17.340 --> 00:54:17.720
Yeah.
是啊。

1297
00:54:17.980 --> 00:54:19.080
So that was hard for me.
所以那对我来说很难。

1298
00:54:19.240 --> 00:54:19.580
Yeah.
是啊。

1299
00:54:19.720 --> 00:54:26.920
Because I had to sort of just put aside all my feelings about tickling and let Pam.
因为我不得不把对挠痒痒的厌恶放在一边，让帕姆去演。

1300
00:54:27.160 --> 00:54:28.020
Ha ha ha ha.
哈哈哈哈。

1301
00:54:28.660 --> 00:54:30.300
Let Pam be won over.
让帕姆被赢得芳心。

1302
00:54:31.040 --> 00:54:35.740
Not by Roy apologizing or hearing her feelings, but simply by tickling her.
不是靠罗伊道歉或倾听她的感受，而只是靠挠她痒痒。

1303
00:54:35.940 --> 00:54:36.700
That's the cure.
这就是解药。

1304
00:54:36.860 --> 00:54:37.260
That's it.
就是这样。

1305
00:54:37.300 --> 00:54:37.640
That's it.
就是这样。

1306
00:54:37.660 --> 00:54:38.560
That's all you got to do.
你只需要做这些。

1307
00:54:38.720 --> 00:54:40.240
You know, she was so serious.
你知道，她以前太严肃了。

1308
00:54:40.620 --> 00:54:41.520
Smile more, Pam.
多笑笑，帕姆。

1309
00:54:41.520 --> 00:54:47.840
Okay, so then the other scene that was really, really hard for me in the series run was in
好的，那么在剧集中对我来说真的、真的很难的另一个场景是在

1310
00:54:47.840 --> 00:54:51.460
season nine, and it's when I had to break down on the phone crying.
第九季，也就是我必须在电话里崩溃大哭的时候。

1311
00:54:51.820 --> 00:54:55.740
You know, it's right before the boom operator comes over and comforts Pam.
你知道，就在收音师过来安慰帕姆之前。

1312
00:54:55.740 --> 00:55:04.780
And what was so hard about that was John and I were separated, so the only thing I had was
那场戏难就难在当时我和约翰分开了，所以我唯一能依靠的就是

1313
00:55:04.780 --> 00:55:06.000
just his voice on a phone.
他在电话里的声音。

1314
00:55:06.280 --> 00:55:07.480
You know, I couldn't see his face.
你知道，我看不见他的脸。

1315
00:55:07.580 --> 00:55:08.740
We couldn't look at each other.
我们无法看着彼此。

1316
00:55:09.280 --> 00:55:11.900
So you couldn't play off the emotion in his face.
所以你无法利用他脸上的情绪来配合表演。

1317
00:55:11.980 --> 00:55:12.700
It was harder.
这就更难了。

1318
00:55:12.900 --> 00:55:13.120
Yeah.
是啊。

1319
00:55:13.120 --> 00:55:17.640
And we did that scene, and he was actually on the phone.
我们拍那场戏时，他确实在线上通电话。

1320
00:55:17.780 --> 00:55:19.060
I was really grateful for that.
我对此真的非常感激。

1321
00:55:19.340 --> 00:55:23.520
That was Kelly Cantley's episode, and she insisted that we be able to hear one another.
那是凯利·坎特利的单集，她坚持认为我们必须能听到彼此的声音。

1322
00:55:23.700 --> 00:55:26.560
She was like, I think he needs to be coming through the phone.
她说，我觉得他需要通过电话传过来。

1323
00:55:26.700 --> 00:55:26.940
Yeah.
是啊。

1324
00:55:27.240 --> 00:55:33.720
But I was having a hard time, and I shared this when we broke down this episode, that
但我当时状态很挣扎，我在拆解这一集时也分享过，

1325
00:55:33.720 --> 00:55:43.060
they actually had John Krasinski go off script, still as Jim, but he got really kind of like
他们实际上让约翰·卡拉辛斯基脱离了剧本，依然保持吉姆的身份，但他变得有点像

1326
00:55:43.060 --> 00:55:46.040
mean Jim in order to help me cry.
那种刻薄的吉姆，为了帮我哭出来。

1327
00:55:46.480 --> 00:55:49.360
Kind of like shock you, like take you back.
有点像吓你一跳，让你措手不及。

1328
00:55:49.720 --> 00:55:49.900
Yeah.
是啊。

1329
00:55:49.900 --> 00:55:50.140
Yeah.
是啊。

1330
00:55:50.260 --> 00:55:54.020
And the thing is, like, you hear about that sometimes when actors do that, and I think
问题是，有时候你会听说演员会这么做，而且我认为

1331
00:55:54.020 --> 00:55:55.760
if it's agreed upon, it's okay.
如果是事先商量好的，那就没问题。

1332
00:55:56.000 --> 00:55:56.980
Like, I disagree.
比如说，我不同意那种做法。

1333
00:55:56.980 --> 00:56:02.440
There's like this famous story from Kramer vs. Kramer where Dustin Hoffman decides to throw
有个关于《克莱默夫妇》的著名故事，达斯汀·霍夫曼决定扔

1334
00:56:02.440 --> 00:56:06.560
a glass—not a breakaway glass, an actual glass—in the middle of a scene with Meryl
一个杯子——不是道具碎玻璃杯，是个真正的玻璃杯——在跟梅尔·斯特里普

1335
00:56:06.560 --> 00:56:09.560
Streep, and it rightfully pissed her off.
对戏的中间，这把她气坏了，这也是情理之中。

1336
00:56:09.820 --> 00:56:09.960
Yeah.
是啊。

1337
00:56:09.980 --> 00:56:14.040
Like, that kind of, like, unsafe kind of, like, to get a reaction.
就那种，有点不太安全的方式，为了得到某种反应。

1338
00:56:14.080 --> 00:56:16.900
It's kind of like, hey, dude, I'll take care of my acting.
这就有点像，嘿，老兄，我自己会演戏。

1339
00:56:17.200 --> 00:56:20.180
Like, I don't need you to shock me into a reaction.
听着，我不需要你吓我一跳来让我做出反应。

1340
00:56:20.420 --> 00:56:22.140
Yeah, you don't need to cut my face.
对，你不需要把我的脸划伤。

1341
00:56:22.280 --> 00:56:22.600
Right.
没错。

1342
00:56:22.740 --> 00:56:22.900
Yeah.
是啊。

1343
00:56:23.120 --> 00:56:27.320
But this was like, hey, John, would you be willing to do this?
但这次是像，嘿，约翰，你愿意这么做吗？

1344
00:56:27.400 --> 00:56:31.040
And he was like, yeah, I'll do it, but you can never use this side of it, because
他说，行，我愿意，但你绝对不能使用这一侧的内容，因为

1345
00:56:31.040 --> 00:56:32.500
it's not what Jim would really say.
这不是吉姆真正会说的话。

1346
00:56:33.280 --> 00:56:34.700
And we were like, agree.
我们当时就说，成交。

1347
00:56:34.880 --> 00:56:36.160
But, like, can you help me?
但是，能帮帮我吗？

1348
00:56:36.260 --> 00:56:39.180
I think if we were in person, it would have been easier, but he really helped me with that
我想如果我们当时面对面会更容易些，但他确实在表演上帮了我大忙。

1349
00:56:39.180 --> 00:56:39.580
performance.
那对我来说真的很难。

1350
00:56:39.580 --> 00:56:40.700
It was really hard for me.
那对我来说真的很难。

1351
00:56:40.840 --> 00:56:41.140
Yeah.
是啊。

1352
00:56:41.380 --> 00:56:42.300
So that was a hard scene.
所以那场戏挺难拍的。

1353
00:56:42.920 --> 00:56:48.160
I think, though, it's great to have, like, scene partners you trust that can help you
不过我觉得，能有像这样可以信任的搭档真的很棒，他们能帮你

1354
00:56:48.160 --> 00:56:53.580
just make that moment, whatever it is, happen, whether it's sad or happy or whatever, you
把那个瞬间——不管是什么情绪，无论是悲伤还是快乐或者别的什么——给演出来，

1355
00:56:53.580 --> 00:56:53.760
know?
对吧？

1356
00:56:53.980 --> 00:56:54.240
Yeah.
对。

1357
00:56:54.440 --> 00:57:00.320
You know, it was always an interesting dance that Phyllis and my character had to do, because
你知道的，菲利丝和我饰演的角色之间总有一种微妙的交锋，因为

1358
00:57:00.320 --> 00:57:02.000
they were true frenemies.
她们是不折不扣的表面朋友、暗中死敌。

1359
00:57:02.340 --> 00:57:05.340
And they would be downright mean to each other.
而且她们有时对彼此真的很刻薄。

1360
00:57:05.740 --> 00:57:11.320
And it was always hard for me to be mean to Phyllis as Angela Kinsey, but very easy for
作为现实中的安吉拉·金西，要我对菲利丝刻薄总是很难，但作为安吉拉·马丁，

1361
00:57:11.320 --> 00:57:13.140
me to be mean to her as Angela Martin.
要我对她刻薄却轻而易举。

1362
00:57:14.560 --> 00:57:16.500
So it was kind of an interesting dynamic.
所以这算是一种挺有趣的化学反应。

1363
00:57:17.360 --> 00:57:19.500
Oh, well, thanks for your question, Ross.
好吧，谢谢你的提问，罗斯。

1364
00:57:19.720 --> 00:57:21.600
And thank you to everyone for listening.
也谢谢大家的收听。

1365
00:57:21.720 --> 00:57:23.000
We hope you enjoyed this episode.
我们希望你们喜欢这期节目。

1366
00:57:23.220 --> 00:57:23.460
Yeah.
是啊。

1367
00:57:23.700 --> 00:57:24.740
We hope you have a great one.
祝你们过得愉快。

1368
00:57:24.820 --> 00:57:25.720
We'll see you next week.
我们下周见。

1369
00:57:25.880 --> 00:57:26.340
See you then.
到时见。

